# Cursor follows the Claude Code sources

This file is a map. The binding text stays in the files it names. Do not copy
those files into `.cursor/`, and do not edit them so Cursor will notice them.

An `@` mention does not inline a file. Read it with your tools. Verified
against [Cursor rules](https://cursor.com/docs/rules) ("Referencing files from
a rule") and [Rules help](https://cursor.com/help/customization/rules). The
same page says this holds for the editor, the CLI, and Cloud Agents.

## Read and obey

Cursor loads some of these by itself. Read any that are not already in your
context, then follow them.

| File | What it is | How Cursor loads it |
|---|---|---|
| `CLAUDE.md` (repo root) | Project doctrine | Auto-loaded, always applied |
| `AGENTS.md` (repo root) | Entry point for agents that do not read `CLAUDE.md` | Auto-loaded, always applied. Nested `AGENTS.md` files apply when working in that directory |
| `.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Scott's working preferences (Australian English, smallest diff, show the command output, discovery before a commit) | Not in the always-applied set. Read it at the start of every session |
| `.claude/AGENTS.md` | Which agent for which job. Not the root `AGENTS.md` | Nested rule: attached when files under `.claude/` are in context. Read it before you choose how work ships |

Loading, verified 2026-11-16:

- [Rules](https://cursor.com/docs/rules): project rules are `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. `alwaysApply: true` is included every chat. A plain `.md` file in that directory is ignored. Root and nested `AGENTS.md` are read; nested files apply to that directory and its children, and the more specific file wins.
- [Rules help](https://cursor.com/help/customization/rules), "How does CLAUDE.md work in Cursor?": Cursor reads `CLAUDE.md` the same way it reads `AGENTS.md`. A root `CLAUDE.md` is always applied, and `alwaysApply` frontmatter does not turn that off.
- This cloud session's always-applied rules were the root `CLAUDE.md` and the root `AGENTS.md` only. Reading a file under `.claude/` attached `.claude/AGENTS.md`. `.claude/CLAUDE.md` was not attached. That is why the row above says to read it.

`VISION.md` wins where docs disagree. That is stated in the root `CLAUDE.md`.

## Rules, skills, and agents

Claude loads `.claude/rules/*.md` when a file matches the rule's `paths`
frontmatter. Cursor does not load that directory. Before you read or edit a
matching file, read the rule. The one that exists today is
`.claude/rules/observability.md` (Sentry, CSP, bundle gate). A glob rule next
to this file attaches a pointer when one of those paths is in context. If
another file appears under `.claude/rules/`, read it when its `paths` match.
Do not copy a new one into `.cursor/rules/` unless its `paths` need a glob
pointer.

Claude loads `.claude/skills/` when a task matches the skill's `description`.
Cursor does not. When the task fits, read that file and follow it. Do not
invent a shorter version.

| When | Read |
|---|---|
| A feature, a bug, or any significant change | `.claude/skills/orchestrate/SKILL.md`. `.claude/skills/feature/SKILL.md` is an alias. Three approval gates: stop and wait. `WORKFLOW.md` allows a hand-built change when the task is small and already specified; say that in the PR, and do not skip a gate the skill says to hold |
| One extraction from a named large file | `.claude/skills/refactor/SKILL.md` |
| Investigate before any code | `.claude/skills/research/SKILL.md` |
| The person you are helping is not Scott | `.claude/skills/collaborate/SKILL.md` before anything else |
| A red or green CI check, or a review comment | `.claude/skills/steward/SKILL.md`. Derive the required set from the ruleset query in that file. Do not memorise it |
| What is breaking in production | `.claude/skills/audit/SKILL.md` |
| A short list of tasks for a gap | `.claude/skills/daily/SKILL.md` |
| Where code goes, or an extraction | `.claude/skills/architecture.md` |
| A Supabase query, a hook, a migration, an Edge Function | `.claude/skills/supabase-patterns.md` |
| A test | `.claude/skills/testing-patterns.md` |
| Load, readiness, zones | `.claude/skills/training-science.md` (doctrine, with the root `CLAUDE.md`) |
| Spawning an agent | Prepend the full `.claude/skills/erg-context.md`. The persona file is under `.claude/agents/`, chosen from `.claude/AGENTS.md` |

`.claude/agent-library/` is parked. Do not load it. `docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md` is
the Codex adapter. It is not the Cursor path.

Shipping is `WORKFLOW.md`: issue, branch, PR, CI. Root `AGENTS.md` names the
things you never do (push to `main`, merge, force-push, Supabase writes,
`--no-verify`, editing `.claude/agents/` or `.claude/agent-library/`).

## Hooks do not run as they do in Claude Code

`.claude/settings.json` wires four command hooks. Cursor does not run that
file for a cloud agent. In the IDE, Claude hooks load only when **Settings →
Agents → Third-Party Imports** ("Include Third-Party Plugins, Skills, and
Other Configs") is on, which is the default. Do not assume they ran. Do the
checks below yourself unless this turn already showed you the hook's output.

Verified 2026-11-16:

- [Third-party hooks](https://cursor.com/docs/reference/third-party-hooks): Claude hooks load from `.claude/settings.json` when that setting is on. `PreToolUse` maps to `preToolUse`, `PostToolUse` to `postToolUse`, `Stop` to `stop`, `SessionStart` to `sessionStart`. `Bash` maps to `Shell`, `Edit` to `Write`. Exit code 2 blocks. `PermissionRequest` and `Notification` have no Cursor hook.
- [Hooks](https://cursor.com/docs/hooks), Cloud agent support: cloud agents run command hooks from `.cursor/hooks.json`, plus Enterprise team and managed hooks. `.claude/settings.json` is not in that source list. `sessionStart` does not run in cloud agents. `beforeShellExecution`, `afterFileEdit`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, and `stop` do. Hooks do not run during an early read-only turn.
- [Cloud Agents](https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent), Hooks support: the same `.cursor/hooks.json` statement. User-level `~/.cursor/hooks.json` is not on the VM.
- A native permission hook (`beforeShellExecution`, `preToolUse`) treats exit 0 with output that is not the permission schema as a **block**. The Claude scripts allow by printing nothing and exiting 0. Pointing a native permission hook at the script would deny every shell command. That is why `.cursor/hooks.json` does not call them directly.
- `postToolUse` can return `additional_context`. `afterFileEdit` documents no output fields. The lint script prints Claude's `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, so a native `afterFileEdit` would drop the findings. A silent lint hook is the failure this repo already had (#295). It is not wired.
- `stop` only documents `followup_message`, which submits a new user message. `warn-uncommitted.sh` prints a user-only `systemMessage` and must not continue the turn. Wiring it would change that contract. It is not wired.

What each hook enforces, and the manual check:

| Hook | Enforces | What you do under Cursor |
|---|---|---|
| `.claude/hooks/session-start.sh` (`SessionStart`) | In a remote Claude session only (`CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE=true`): warn if `deno` is missing, then `npm ci --prefix web` so the lockfile is not rewritten. Elsewhere it exits 0 | Cloud agents do not run `sessionStart`. If `web/node_modules` is missing before lint, test, or build, run `npm ci --prefix web`. Do not `npm install`. If you are on an Edge Function and `deno` is missing, say so |
| `.claude/hooks/block-secret-commit.sh` (`PreToolUse` / `Bash`) | Blocks `git commit` when a staged path matches the pattern in that script (exit 2) | Wired, below. Still read the staged list before you commit. The pattern lives only in the script |
| `.claude/hooks/lint-edited-file.sh` (`PostToolUse` / `Edit\|Write`) | Advisory ESLint on a `.js` / `.jsx` file under `web/src` or `web/scripts`. Findings are context, not a failed edit | After such an edit, run `web/node_modules/.bin/eslint --max-warnings=0 --no-warn-ignored` on that file. Fix findings, or show them, before you finish. `npm run lint` in `web/` is the full check |
| `.claude/hooks/warn-uncommitted.sh` (`Stop`) | Tells the user when the turn ends dirty. Silent in a remote Claude session. Does not continue the turn | Before you finish, `git status --porcelain`. Uncommitted work goes in the commit or is named in the PR body |

`.cursor/hooks.json` wires one adapter, `.cursor/hooks/block-secret-commit.sh`,
on `beforeShellExecution` with matcher `git commit`. The adapter runs the
Claude script and turns its silence into `{"permission":"allow"}`, and its
exit 2 into a deny. The deny sentence is the script's own wording, repeated
so Cursor has it on stdout. The path pattern is not repeated. Both the IDE
and cloud agents run this hook (`beforeShellExecution` is in the cloud
matrix). It does not run during a read-only cloud turn, and an IDE with
third-party import may also run the Claude `PreToolUse` hook on the same
commit. The Claude script remains the check.

Husky is separate, and it only runs when `core.hooksPath` is `.husky`. Cursor
cloud agents point that elsewhere, so run the commands yourself when they
apply:

- `.husky/pre-commit` — `cd web && npx lint-staged`
- `.husky/pre-push` — needs `origin/main`, then `cd web && npx vitest run --changed origin/main --passWithNoTests`

Never `--no-verify` without an explicit reason.

## `settings.json` permissions

`.claude/settings.json` has `permissions.allow` and `permissions.ask`. It has
no `deny` list. Cursor does not enforce either key.

`ask` is `git push`, `git reset`, and `rm`. Treat `git reset` and `rm` as
stop-and-ask unless the user explicitly requested that command. `git push`
only the branch this task told you to publish, never `main`.

The stops that are absolute live in the root `AGENTS.md` and the root
`CLAUDE.md` (no Supabase writes, no migration apply, no merge, no
force-push except `--force-with-lease` on your own branch). An empty `deny`
list does not lift them.
